      "html": "<button class=\"ds-pill\"><span class=\"ds-pill-dot\"></span><span><b>3</b> automations on</span><svg width=\"16\" height=\"16\" viewBox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" stroke=\"currentColor\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\" stroke-linejoin=\"round\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><path d=\"m9 18 6-6-6-6\"/></svg></button>",
      "css": ".ds-pill{--n0:#0c0c0f;--n1:#131317;--n2:#1c1c22;--n3:#26262e;--n4:#33333d;--n5:#4a4a56;--n6:#74737f;--n7:#a5a4b1;--n9:#ecebf2;--line:#24242b;--ok:#8fd468;--foe:#ee8130;--font-ui:'Figtree',system-ui,sans-serif;--font-fig:'Barlow Semi Condensed','Figtree',system-ui,sans-serif;--ease:cubic-bezier(.16,1,.3,1);}.ds-pill{display:flex;align-items:center;gap:10px;width:320px;min-height:44px;padding:0 10px 0 14px;border:0;border-radius:22px;background:var(--n2);color:var(--n7);font:500 14px/1.2 var(--font-ui);cursor:pointer}.ds-pill b{color:var(--n9);font-weight:600}.ds-pill svg{margin-left:auto}.ds-pill-dot{width:8px;height:8px;border-radius:50%;background:var(--ok)}.ds-pill:hover{background:var(--n3)}.ds-pill:focus-visible{outline:2px solid var(--n9);outline-offset:2px}"
    }
  ],
  "narrative": {
    "northStar": "Trading card anatomy without the card rectangle",
    "overview": "The interface is a quiet, dark, neutral instrument. Everything the player operates (rows, buttons, tabs, sheets) is drawn from one fixed neutral ramp, and the only saturated colour on screen is the energy colour of whichever Pokémon or type is being shown: a radial halo behind the foe's sprite, its HP bar, the energy dots beside its types. Information is laid out the way a trading card reads (name left, HP figures right, type below, figures in pairs), but there is no card rectangle: modules are open sections separated by hairline seams on a single dark ground.\n\nDensity is high and phone-first: one player, short one-handed check-ins, 44px tap targets, edge-to-edge sections with a 16px gutter. Importance is carried by a fixed size ramp in a condensed figure face, not by colour. Meaning colours (ok, warn, bad) appear only as text and small marks, never as button fills.\n\n**Scope and mergeability.** This system is a layer over the upstream PokeClicker client. Every rule is scoped under `html.rd`, so switching the redesign off restores the classic interface untouched. Upstream Bootstrap 4 markup and module roots are restyled and relocated into the six pages at runtime, never rewritten; new surfaces should follow the same approach (restyle upstream classes and attribute hooks under `html.rd`, add `rd-` markup only in the shell).",
    "keyCharacteristics": [
      "One dark ground (n1) with tonal steps for controls; no white surfaces.",
      "Saturated colour belongs to content (type energy), never to chrome.",
      "Hairline 1px seams between rows instead of boxes.",
      "Barlow Semi Condensed for names and every figure (tabular), Figtree for UI text.",
      "State marks are typographic: ● caught, ✶ shiny.",
      "The fight is always on screen: docked column on desktop, mini combat bar above the tabs on phones."
    ],
    "rules": [
      {
        "name": "The Energy Belongs to Content Rule",
        "body": "Saturated hue appears only on what the player is looking at (the Pokémon, its type, its HP). Chrome, controls and navigation stay on the neutral ramp.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Fixed Ramp Rule",
        "body": "The nine neutral steps and the seam colour are the only tonal tokens. New surfaces pick a step; they do not mix new greys.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Meaning-as-Text Rule",
        "body": "ok, warn and bad colour text and small marks. A button never gets a coloured fill; an upstream `btn-danger` becomes an n2 button with coral text.",
        "section": "colors"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Figures Are Condensed Rule",
        "body": "Every number on screen is Barlow Semi Condensed with tabular figures, so columns align and values don't jitter as the game ticks.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Size Carries Importance Rule",
        "body": "Hierarchy comes from the fixed size ramp and weight, not from colour.",
        "section": "typography"
      },
      {
        "name": "The Flat Ground Rule",
        "body": "Anything that sits on the page is flat. A shadow only appears on something floating above it, and it is always ambient and blurred, never a hard offset.",
        "section": "elevation"
      }
    ],
    "dos": [
      "Do scope every new rule under `html.rd` and restyle upstream Bootstrap 4 classes and attribute hooks rather than editing upstream templates.",
      "Do take every tonal value from the n0–n9 ramp and every divider from the seam colour (#24242b, 1px).",
      "Do route saturated colour through `--foe` / `--foe-2` or the type energy table, and only onto content.",
      "Do set every number in Barlow Semi Condensed with tabular figures.",
      "Do keep tap targets at 44px minimum and the 16px page gutter.",
      "Do honour `prefers-reduced-motion`: sheets and halo transitions switch off."
    ],
    "donts": [
      "Don't put a white or light surface anywhere, or bring back the decorative background.",
      "Don't fill a button, tab or chip with a meaning or energy colour; meaning lives in text and small marks.",
      "Don't wrap modules in bordered card rectangles; use open sections and hairline seams.",
      "Don't cast a shadow from anything resting on the page; shadows belong to floating layers only.",
      "Don't add a second emphasis level of buttons; there is one tonal button.",
      "Don't replace drawn icons with text glyphs (such as \"?\"); interface icons come from the Lucide sprite."
    ]
  }
}